    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Clement Herron Real Estate is delighted to welcome No. 45 Glen Vale, Ballyragget, Co. Kilkenny to the sales market.\r\n\r\nConstructed in 2005, this superbly presented five-bedroom detached residence extends to approximately 155 sq. m. and offers an exceptional amount of living and bedroom accommodation over two floors. Presented in showroom condition throughout, the property is bright, spacious and beautifully maintained, with an excellent layout ideally suited to modern family living.\r\n\r\nFrom the moment you arrive, No. 45 makes an excellent first impression. The distinctive exterior is complemented by an extensive cobblelock driveway, providing generous private off-street parking while creating a smart, low-maintenance frontage with excellent kerb appeal. Gated access is provided to both sides of the residence, leading through to the rear garden.\r\n\r\nInternally, the sense of space and natural light is immediately apparent. The ground-floor accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall, sitting room, substantial kitchen/dining area, utility room, guest W.C. and a ground-floor fifth bedroom, providing excellent flexibility for a growing family, home office, guest accommodation or playroom.\r\n\r\nPositioned to the front of the property, the sitting room is a warm and inviting space with a solid oak timber floor and an attractive cast-iron fireplace with granite hearth and solid-fuel stove, creating a particularly appealing focal point.\r\n\r\nThe layout flows naturally from the sitting room towards the kitchen and dining accommodation, giving the principal living areas a connected and sociable feel while still retaining clearly defined spaces.\r\n\r\nThe kitchen/dining room forms the heart of the home and is particularly impressive in terms of both its proportions and natural light. French doors overlook and open directly onto the rear garden, allowing sunlight to pour into the room and creating an excellent connection between the indoor and outdoor spaces.\r\n\r\nThe kitchen is fitted with an extensive range of attractive units and generous worktop space, together with a breakfast bar, providing an informal dining area in addition to the main dining space. Integrated appliances include a dishwasher, double oven, hob and extractor fan. The tiled flooring throughout this area is both practical and well suited to busy family life.\r\n\r\nA separate utility room provides valuable additional storage and functionality and is fitted with a range of maple units, providing excellent additional cupboard and worktop space while complementing the quality and finish of the main kitchen. The downstairs W.C. and fifth bedroom further enhance the versatility of the ground-floor accommodation.\r\n\r\nThe first floor is equally impressive and continues the bright and airy character found throughout the house. There are four generously proportioned double bedrooms, offering excellent accommodation for larger families without compromising on bedroom size.\r\n\r\nThe primary bedroom benefits from its own en-suite bathroom, while the remaining bedrooms are served by a spacious family bathroom. Large windows throughout the upper floor maximise natural light, giving the landing and bedrooms a particularly fresh and welcoming atmosphere.\r\n\r\nThe property has been maintained to an excellent standard, with attractive details including solid pine internal doors, skirting boards and architraves adding warmth and character throughout. The house also benefits from gas-fired central heating.\r\n\r\nExternally, the property offers an excellent balance between attractive presentation and low-maintenance practicality. In addition to the substantial cobblelock parking area to the front, there is gated access on both sides of the residence.\r\n\r\nTo the rear lies a large private garden extending to approximately 130 sq. m. The garden is predominantly laid in lawn and securely enclosed with fencing to both sides, creating a private and practical outdoor space.\r\n\r\nThe generous lawn provides ample room for children to play, while the size and layout offer excellent potential for outdoor dining, summer barbecues and entertaining. French doors from the dining area provide direct access to the garden, making the outdoor space feel like a natural extension of the main living accommodation.\r\n\r\nThe rear elevation also benefits from a useful paved area immediately adjoining the house, while the wide lawn and secure boundaries make this a particularly attractive feature for families and purchasers seeking meaningful outdoor space without an excessive level of maintenance.\r\n\r\nLOCATION: \r\n\r\nLocation is another major advantage of No. 45 Glen Vale. The property is situated in the small town of Ballyragget, Co. Kilkenny, conveniently positioned on the N77 and providing excellent access to Kilkenny City and the surrounding towns of Durrow, Castlecomer and Carlow.\r\n\r\nKilkenny City is approximately 18 km away, placing the city within comfortable commuting distance for employment, schools, shopping, restaurants, leisure facilities and the extensive range of services associated with Kilkenny City.\r\n\r\nAbbeyleix is 15km away, Durrow is approximately 9 km away, while Castlecomer is also approximately 9 km from Ballyragget, making both towns readily accessible for everyday amenities and employment.\r\n\r\nDublin is 115km from the property, Carlow is approximately 31 km away, further extending the range of employment, educational and commercial centres accessible from the property.\r\n\r\nBallyragget itself provides an excellent selection of everyday amenities, allowing purchasers to enjoy the convenience of village living without having to travel into Kilkenny for every requirement. Local amenities include shopping, pharmacy, medical and dental services, cafés and pubs, community facilities, primary education and childcare facilities.\r\n\r\nThe combination of village amenities and accessibility to Kilkenny City, Castlecomer, Durrow and Carlow makes the location particularly practical for families and commuters alike.\r\n\r\nWith approximately 155 sq. m. of internal accommodation, five bedrooms, three bathrooms, extensive off-street parking and an approximately 130 sq. m. rear garden, No. 45 offers considerably more space than may initially be apparent from the front elevation.\r\n\r\nThe standard of presentation is equally noteworthy. This is a home that can be occupied and enjoyed immediately, without the requirement for significant refurbishment or modernisation.\r\n\r\nVIEWINGS ARE STRICTLY BY APPOINMENT ONLY!\r\nNo. 45 Glen Vale is a superbly presented, exceptionally spacious detached family residence offering excellent living accommodation, five bedrooms, generous private parking and a substantial enclosed rear garden in a highly convenient location.\r\n\r\nThe combination of space, condition, natural light and a versatile family-friendly layout makes this a property that is sure to impress.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the quality, proportions and excellent condition of this beautiful family home."
      },
